-- Q1187: Fund-to-Government-Wide Reconciliation [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 77, reconciliation is required because governmental funds use the current financial resources measurement focus and modified accrual basis, while government-wide statements use the economic resources measurement focus and full accrual basis. These different frameworks create systematic reporting gaps for long-term assets and liabilities.
Wrong (A): Both governmental fund and government-wide statements use the same fiscal year-end. Different year-ends do not drive the reconciliation requirement.
Wrong (C): While government-wide statements do exclude fiduciary funds, this is not the primary reason reconciliation is required between fund and government-wide statements.
Wrong (D): Fund statements use modified accrual, not cash basis. Government-wide statements use full accrual, but the distinction is modified accrual versus full accrual.$EXPL$
