Wrong (A): Capital outlays are not subtracted. They are added back because the fund-level expenditure treatment is reversed when assets are capitalized government-wide.
Wrong (C): Capital outlays appear as expenditures in fund statements but as capital assets in government-wide statements, so they do not appear identically in both.
Wrong (D): Capital outlays are capitalized as assets, not reported as deferred outflows of resources. Deferred outflows have a separate, specific definition under GASB 63.$EXPL$
