-- Q1196: Interfund Transactions [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 34, paragraph 112, interfund loans are classified as reciprocal interfund activities because both funds exchange value. One fund provides cash and records a receivable while the other receives cash and records a payable, mirroring an arm''s-length transaction.
Wrong (A): Transfers are nonreciprocal activities representing one-directional resource flows. They are reported as other financing sources and uses, not as reciprocal exchanges.
Wrong (B): Reimbursements are corrections of initial charges to the wrong fund. They are nonreciprocal because they restore the paying fund rather than creating an exchange.
Wrong (D): Annual allocations are nonreciprocal transfers of resources without an equivalent exchange of value between funds.$EXPL$
