Wrong (A): Derived tax revenues arise from underlying exchange transactions between third parties, such as sales taxes or income taxes. Property taxes have no underlying exchange.
Wrong (C): Government-mandated nonexchange transactions involve one government requiring another to spend resources on a specific program, such as federal mandates on states.
